cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use IPFD in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "IPFD: Isaac Policy Failure Debugger"
abstract: >-
  A headless debugging utility for robot-policy rollouts in Isaac Lab that
  localizes the recovery-controller-relative point after which a provided
  recovery controller no longer succeeds from restored simulator branches, and
  reports whether any internal signal predicted the failure before it was
  externally observable. Scope is Franka Emika Panda single-object
  pick-and-place. The project is archived as an honest negative: a preregistered
  five-seed study found that restored branches with equal exposed state,
  equal immediate observations, and identical replayed actions can still reverse
  the downstream task decision, and that restoring additional exposed runtime
  state reduced but did not eliminate that disagreement. See
  ARCHIVED_NEGATIVE_RESULT.md.
type: software
